pyserial(The digital pipeline between your computer and the board. It constantly pings the Arduino over USB to pull live X/Y axis values and button clicks, translating raw analog signals into data your script can actually use)
pyautogui(The puppet master library that steals your system’s pointer. It captures the direction vector from the joystick and violently moves your mouse around the screen, clicking whenever you press the stick button)
Copy this into the dev consoel in visual studio//pip install pyautogui pyserial
